A||||4||rodmcneill||88 Front Wheel Bearings||||1||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||05-30-2001||12:09 AM||||Well after seeing some posts on the unavailability of 88 front wheel bearings, I decided to do some investigating. On a couple of posts I have seen the Timken part #513040 mentioned as the replacement wheel bearing (not the complete hub carrier) I called two local bearing supply houses and gave them the part#. First one told me they had no listing for that part#. Second one had no info. either but said he would call Timken and get back to me. Timken stated they had supplied the bearings to GM who pressed them into the castings and then sent them back to Timken. They stated they will not sell the bearing itself because of liability concerns(I guess they don't trust us with a press) I have a low mileage 88 myself so this is not a concern right now but in the future...I would be very surprised if this bearing is not used in another application. Has anyone on the forum tried to get this bearing, not through auto supply houses but rather through bearing supply houses?||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||05-30-2001||12:58 PM||||That's the number I ordered from Autozone online a couple of months ago. It's a complete hub assembly. Cost is $92.99 each. I just checked and they show them in stock still.<P>The local NAPA store said they could still get the assembly (not sure about brand though) but wanted something like $150 each.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||05-30-2001||01:27 PM||||$92.99 is an excellent price. I ordered one through Advance Auto, last summer. Cost like $139. <BR>I would expect $150 from NAPA, if they can get them. They are usually high. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||05-30-2001||08:06 PM||||My front bearings are still good but when I removed my front suspension on my 50,000-mile formula I found out that the rear dust cover was starting to rot through. It had a pin hole in it. If I had not caught this than the front wheel bearings would have got water and debris in there and the bearing would have surely failed. You better check yours. Low mileage means nothing.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||rodmcneill||05-30-2001||09:33 PM||||Thanks, 88formula, I will check mine.||||reg||1
